Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: python/libxml.c
Line: 2794
Function: libxml_saveNodeTo
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: If a non-document node with node->doc == NULL (e.g., created via xmlNewNode and not attached to a document) is passed, doc is set to node->doc and then dereferenced at doc->type without a NULL check, causing a NULL pointer dereference. This is reachable by calling libxml_xmlNewNode followed by libxml_saveNodeTo on the returned node.

Source context:
```c
